Exact-pin `xgrammar` and `sentencepiece` to the versions SGLang's pyproject pins,
because the image does not honour those pins on its own.

SGLang v0.5.21 tightened two pins in python/pyproject.toml:

  "xgrammar==0.2.7",        (was ==0.2.1; #39026, XGrammar V4.1 DSML constraints)
  "sentencepiece==0.2.1",   (was unpinned; 0.2.2 rejects null pieces in InternVL
                             tokenizers, cherry-pick #41788)

Why the image would otherwise miss them:

  * Dockerfile.sglang-nightly installs `xgrammar` UNPINNED in the "remaining
    deps" step, so it resolves to PyPI latest (0.2.8 on 2026-10-03).
  * stages/missing_deps.py only checks PRESENCE of a dependency, never its
    version, so it leaves whatever an earlier step installed in place. The same
    applies to sentencepiece if anything earlier pulls it in unpinned (0.2.2 is
    the current latest, i.e. exactly the release upstream pins away from).

  ARG XGRAMMAR_VERSION=""       # empty = leave xgrammar as resolved (older recipes)
  ARG SENTENCEPIECE_VERSION=""  # empty = leave sentencepiece as resolved
  XGRAMMAR_VERSION=0.2.7        # in sglang-0.5.21-sm121.recipe and later
  SENTENCEPIECE_VERSION=0.2.1   # in sglang-0.5.21-sm121.recipe and later

Same mechanism as dockerfile-tokenizers-pin.patch: gated `uv pip install
--no-deps` in the builder stage, before the dist-packages split, so it is carried
into the runtime stage. --no-deps is safe here: sentencepiece has no runtime
dependencies, and xgrammar 0.2.7's (apache-tvm-ffi>=0.1.10, pydantic, torch,
transformers, numpy, typing-extensions) are a subset of what 0.2.8 already
required (apache-tvm-ffi>=0.1.11), so they are satisfied by the time this runs and
the step can change exactly the two pinned packages. aarch64 wheels exist on PyPI
for both (xgrammar 0.2.7 cp312, sentencepiece 0.2.1).

PLACEMENT: LAST in the builder stage, applied AFTER dockerfile-tokenizers-pin.patch
in apply_patches(). The hunk is TRAILING-CONTEXT-ONLY (anchored on the upstream
dist-packages split block), so it lands directly before the split regardless of
which optional dockerfile-*.patch steps ran before it.

NOT YET VALIDATED in a built image. After the 0.5.21-sm121 build check
`pip list | grep -iE 'xgrammar|sentencepiece'` and that `import sglang` plus
srt.entrypoints.http_server still import.

Remove once SGLang's own pins are honoured by the resolve (i.e. once
missing_deps.py compares versions, or the upstream Dockerfile pins xgrammar).

Apply to: container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly in the local clone of
scitrera/cuda-containers.

--- a/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
+++ b/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
@@ -523,3 +523,18 @@
+# dgxarley: exact-pin xgrammar / sentencepiece; missing_deps.py checks presence only, so the unpinned install above wins.
+ARG XGRAMMAR_VERSION=""
+ARG SENTENCEPIECE_VERSION=""
+RUN --mount=type=cache,id=uv-cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \
+    if [ -n "$XGRAMMAR_VERSION" ]; then \
+        echo "=== Pinning xgrammar==${XGRAMMAR_VERSION} ==="; \
+        uv pip install --no-deps "xgrammar==${XGRAMMAR_VERSION}"; \
+        python3 -c "import importlib.metadata as m, xgrammar; print('xgrammar', m.version('xgrammar'))"; \
+    fi; \
+    if [ -n "$SENTENCEPIECE_VERSION" ]; then \
+        echo "=== Pinning sentencepiece==${SENTENCEPIECE_VERSION} ==="; \
+        uv pip install --no-deps "sentencepiece==${SENTENCEPIECE_VERSION}"; \
+        python3 -c "import importlib.metadata as m, sentencepiece; print('sentencepiece', m.version('sentencepiece'))"; \
+    fi
+
 # Break up dist-packages into smaller layers to avoid hitting Docker layer size limits
 COPY stages/directory_split2.sh /opt/directory_split2.sh
 RUN chmod +x /opt/directory_split2.sh && \
